MANUAL CHECKS (constitution point numbers cited)

#1 Structure — full-page heading context: `grep -n "<h[1-6]" web/templates/pages/whatif.html
web/templates/components/whatif/guardrails.html` → h1 (whatif.html:5, page title) → h2
(guardrails.html:4, "Spending...") → h3 (spending_optimizer.html:8,
"How much can I spend?") → h4 (results outcome / "Complete tested frontier") → h5 (per-option
name / per-frontier "planned"/"flexible" heading) → h4 (spending-graph-heading). No skipped
levels; de-nesting h5→h4 between sibling sections is normal document structure, not a skip.
PASS.

#2 Data tables — server-rendered frontier table
(spending_optimizer_results.html:40-51) uses `<th scope="col">` for all seven columns plus
`<th scope="row">` on the Base-budget column; `<caption>` present. JS-built tables
(`makeTable()`, whatif-spending-optimizer.js:279-304) use `<th scope="col">` for the header
row only (no `scope="row"` on the leading Plan-year/Calendar-month column) — simple tables
with column headers are sufficient under 1.3.1/1.3.2 for this shape of data (no
cross-referenced row+column identification needed) so this is not a FAIL; flagged as an
OBSERVATION for parity with the server table's convention. No layout tables found.

#3 Buttons/links — every actionable control in scope is a native `<button>` (Inspect, Apply,
Compare, Cancel, Close evidence, view/dollars are native `<select>`) inside real `<form>`
elements where the action is a submission (data-spending-apply-form). No `<div onclick>`.

#4/#6 Labels & stated requirements — every input has an associated `<label for=...>`; the
boost checkbox's required-state is stated in VISIBLE text
(`#spending-boost-required`, unhidden only while `boostEnabled.checked`) and wired via
`aria-describedby` on both dependent fields; advanced-search fields share visible help text
stating "today's US dollars per month" via `aria-describedby="spending-search-money-help"`.
Verified live: `boostRequiredVisible: true` after keyboard-enabling the boost checkbox.

#5 Validation announcement — native `reportValidity()`/`.focus()` on the first invalid field
(prepare()/submit handler); server/apply errors are written into
`#spending-optimizer-status[role=status][aria-live=polite]` and the error or outcome node is
explicitly focused after swap (`handleHTMXAfterSwap`, JS lines 599-606; submit handler lines
542-548). Traced in source, consistent with prior verdict's trace.

#7/#12 Contrast, both themes — sampled via real computed styles in the browser (page.evaluate
getComputedStyle), function documented in audit.cjs:
  light: help-text 7.63:1, rule-text 15.17:1, run-button (white/indigo-700) 6.29:1,
