  dark:  help-text 10.18:1, rule-text 13.9:1, run-button 6.29:1, cancel-button-disabled 13.9:1,
         range-box 8.18:1, boost-help 10.18:1, frontier-caption 10.18:1, apply-button 6.29:1
  All ≥ 4.5:1 (text) and the 3:1 UI/large-text floor. Plotly gridline stroke vs. actual
  transparent-composited background: light 4.34:1 (`rgb(107,114,128)` on white), dark 8.33:1
  (`rgb(168,162,158)` on `rgb(41,37,36)`) — both clear the constitution's 3:1 chart-stroke
  floor (this is the exact defect class attempt-1's checker-a11y verdict FAILed at 1.49/1.99:1;
  current code — `grid: dark ? '#a8a29e' : '#6b7280'`, whatif-spending-optimizer.js:243 — is
  fixed and re-verified independently here, not just taken on the prior verdict's word).
  Dark-mode chart re-theme is LIVE, not just CSS: toggled `document.documentElement.classList
  .add('dark')` on an already-rendered chart and re-read `data[2].line.color`:
  light `#1d4ed8` → dark `#93c5fd` (theme() + MutationObserver-driven refreshTheme()).

#8 Color alone — "Qualifies"/"Did not qualify" rendered as literal text (not color-only);
warning/positive banners pair color classes with full sentence text. PASS.

#9 Keyboard — full keyboard-only path exercised and passing in the harness: focus
`#spending-boost-details > summary` → Enter (opens disclosure) → check boost checkbox → fill
required fields → fill minimum → focus `#spending-optimizer-run` → Enter → results render and
`[data-spending-outcome]` receives focus (`outcomeFocused: true`) → focus first Inspect
button → Enter → graph opens and `#spending-graph-heading` receives focus
(`graphHeadingFocused: true`) → focus "Chart values, samples, and events" summary → Enter →
table becomes visible (`chartTableVisible: 1`). No `outline:none` found; every interactive
element in scope carries `focus:outline focus:outline-2 focus:outline-accent` (or
`-offset-2` variant).

#10 Focus after swap — confirmed above (#5); "Evidence closed. Nothing was saved." /
"Comparison cancelled. Nothing was saved." / "Spending option saved..." are all routed through
the single `role=status aria-live=polite` region; destructive/state actions (cancel, apply,
close) each set a distinct, non-empty status message.

#11 Chart text alternative — every Plotly host div is `role="img"` with a descriptive
`aria-label` naming the adjacent table (e.g. "Spending evidence chart; exact values are in the
adjacent chart values table"), immediately followed by a `<p>` takeaway summary and a
`<details>`-collapsed data table built from the SAME series the chart plots
(`makeTable`/`simulatedView`/`worstView`/`timelineView`/`baseView`, whatif-spending-optimizer.js
:306-434). Verified the tick-thinning change does NOT drop table rows: `chartLayout`'s
`maxYearTicks`/`yearStep` only feed `xaxis.dtick` (axis labels); every renderer builds its table
from `series.years`/`timeline.annual_averages`/`timeline.months` directly, independent of the
axis math. Isolated the tick formula at both extremes: 375px width → maxYearTicks=4,
yearStep=10 (3 ticks shown for a 30-year span); 1440px → maxYearTicks=10, yearStep=4 (8 ticks
shown) — both respect the documented `Math.min(10, ...)` bound and neither collapses to 0/degenerate
step.

